B = [
('Thermos','Europe','1900s-present','housewares','In the style of Thermos, sturdy insulated-ware design with smooth cylindrical and softly rounded forms. Polished and brushed stainless steel is paired with matte powder-coated finishes in charcoal, black, navy, forest green and a signature bright red accent, with white and silver for contrast. Surfaces are clean and seamless with a slight sheen, thin metal rims and small moulded black or red details. The mark is a bold, wide, red capital wordmark inside or beside a simple rectangular or oval frame, with tidy printed text in plain sans-serif. Occasional kids prints in cheerful cartoon colours and vintage plaid or enamel tones. Dependable, no-nonsense, practical and warm.'),
('Opinel','Europe','1890s-present','tools','In the style of Opinel, rustic French craft simplicity. Slim, tapered, teardrop-like forms in pale natural beech wood, olivewood and dark stained wood with a clear lacquer glow, joined to plain carbon steel that develops a soft grey patina. Small touches of colour in navy, olive, red, yellow and white lacquer. The emblem is a small crowned open hand with a plain serif capital wordmark and the words Savoie France in a thin line below, usually in navy blue or black on a cream, white or deep blue field. Kraft card, tin and cardboard packing in blue and cream, with simple fine rules. Honest, modest, countryside and timeless.'),
('Leatherman','North America','1980s-present','tools','In the style of Leatherman, tough, dense, precision-machined industrial design. Brushed and bead-blasted stainless steel, black oxide and matte black coatings are paired with a strong yellow or gold accent and occasional anodised colour in orange, blue or olive. Forms are compact, rectangular and softly bevelled, with rows of small perforated holes, crisp stamped edges, visible rivets and tight seams. The mark is a bold capital wordmark in wide, heavy, slightly squared sans-serif, often set beside a bold geometric letter L emblem inside a rounded square, in black and yellow. Black matte boxes and sleeves with thin yellow lettering. Utilitarian, rugged and confident.'),
('Maglite','North America','1980s-present','tools','In the style of Maglite, robust machined-aluminium design with a heavy, solid feel. Perfectly round cylindrical forms with fine diamond knurling, thick walls, crisp bevels and visible machining lines. Finishes are hard-anodised matte black as the core, with silver, titanium grey, deep red, blue and olive variants and small engraved capital lettering along the surface. The mark is a bold black wordmark in chunky, rounded, slightly squashed capitals with a hyphen-like gap, paired with a round shield-like emblem containing a swooping curved cut. Black and white packing with plain, strong graphics. Tough, dependable, no-frills and industrial.'),
('Burton','North America','1990s-present','sports','In the style of Burton, bold alpine-rebel graphics built on stark black and white. The emblem is a jagged, snow-capped mountain silhouette with a pointed peak in white on black, with a heavy wide capital wordmark beneath. An older emblem is a chunky interlocked letter B form in thick rounded black strokes. Palette is black, white and grey, then clashing neon pink, acid green, orange, cyan and purple in colour-blocked panels. Surfaces are glossy and slick with graphic prints of skulls, flames, camouflage, geometric shards and tropical foliage, plus matte technical nylon and fleece. Forms are loose, oversized and chunky with sharp angular cuts.'),
('Quiksilver','Oceania','1970s-present','surfwear','In the style of Quiksilver, surf-culture graphics built around a logo of a large curling wave overlapping a snow-capped mountain peak, drawn as a bold black or single-colour silhouette inside a rounded or square badge. The wordmark is a lowercase, flowing, hand-brushed script, sometimes chrome-gradient or glitchy blue and silver on faded black or white. Palette is washed black, charcoal, bone white, sky blue, sea green, red and sandy tan, with vivid tropical tones for retro pieces. Surfaces carry cracked screen prints, painted brush strokes, hibiscus and palm patterns, tribal flames and horizontal band stripes. Fabrics feel soft, sun-faded, garment-dyed, relaxed and loose.'),
('Rip Curl','Oceania','1960s-present','fashion','In the style of Rip Curl, rugged Australian wave-riding graphics. The emblem is a swirling spiral wave curl drawn as a round or oval badge, with a wordmark in tall, narrow, hand-drawn capitals. Palette is faded oranges, sky blue, teal, mustard, sage, cream, black and coral, often garment-dyed with soft chalky tones and contrast stitching in cream. Surface graphics are retro beach club badges, sun and palm illustrations, skulls, roses, waves and tropical flowers in distressed screen-print layers. Black neoprene-like panels trimmed in bright colour contrast with soft brushed cotton and fleece surfaces. Sun-bleached, relaxed, adventurous and salty.'),
('Billabong','Oceania','1970s-present','surfwear','In the style of Billabong, sunny, relaxed beach-culture graphics. The mark is a rounded, wavy, hand-drawn wordmark with a flowing wave line, often placed inside a rounded rectangle badge with slanted parallel slash lines. Palette is muted sage, teal, deep navy, sand, cream, burnt orange and warm brown, with brighter aqua, coral and lime for retro tones. Surface designs include circular sunburst and wave rings, hand-drawn landscape line illustrations, tropical flowers, stripes and tie-dye washes in soft, faded screen print. Textures are soft garment-washed cotton, quick-dry nylon and slub knit with contrast stitching and small woven labels. Easygoing, sporty and sun-faded.'),
('Dickies','North America','1920s-present','workwear','In the style of Dickies, hard-wearing American workwear identity. The emblem is a bold oval badge with a thick white rim and a slim red and yellow ring, a deep blue centre and a wide, italic, outlined capital script wordmark in white, also seen in black and white or vintage brown and gold woven versions. Palette is khaki, black, navy, charcoal, olive and stone, with the red, yellow and royal blue badge as the single bright accent. Fabrics are smooth, tightly woven twill with a slight sheen, crisp pressed finish, bar-tack stitching and plain flat seams. Clean, neat, sturdy, blue-collar and street-ready.'),
('Alpha Industries','North America','1950s-present','military','In the style of Alpha Industries, military-surplus design with a clean technical edge. The emblem is a bold, stylised capital A built from angular parallel wedges and a tall triangle, over a small wide-spaced capital wordmark, shown as a woven rectangular patch or a black rubber patch. Palette is olive green, sage, black, navy, sand and camouflage prints, with signature bright orange and red as an accent in linings and tags. Surfaces are glossy nylon, matte ripstop, rubbery coated finish and soft ribbed knit with stencilled lettering, hook-and-loop patches and small red pull tags. Disciplined, functional, cold-war aviation heritage and understated.'),
]
